R1b CLAUDE REVISED POSITION (independent, sealed)

PROMISE (merged): "Prove you can be trusted in close, readable fights, and the settlement's routes and services change because of the order you chose to fix them."

KEEP FROM CODEX: contract -> route -> single expedition slot -> atomic delivery -> visible service change; failure with no progression debt and objective reset at source; first slice = 1 hub, 2 short routes, 2 contracts, 2 service changes, 1 enemy kit x 2 behaviours.

DESIGN RULE THAT ANSWERS THE CHECKLIST RISK: every service change must alter a ROUTE, a THREAT or a TOOL, never only decoration.
- route: a repaired gate opens a shorter path that bypasses a watched crossing (less risk, less salvage).
- threat: a restored lookout reveals where opponents wait before you leave (information changes the plan).
- tool: a reopened stall sells one consumable that changes a fight (a smoke pot that breaks an opponent's lock-on; a salve usable only out of combat).
The test is the player saying "I took the gate route because..." not "I got more gold".

COMBAT FOR THE SLICE (rules-first, smallest set that carries the promise):
- Verbs: move, strike (2-hit string + a heavy), guard (hold, faces the target, no height), throw (beats guard), cast (one elemental cast available from the first second on a cooldown; never gated behind melee).
- Melee feeds magic, not the reverse: landed strikes and well-timed guards shorten the cast cooldown and, at full charge, upgrade the next cast to its charged form. A pure caster can still play; a fighter who reads well casts more.
- Triangle resolved with explicit rules: guard beats strike (chip only); throw beats guard (break + paired throw); strike beats throw (the throw has a visible 0.3 s reach-in that a strike interrupts). Mutual throws = both stagger back. Throws need open space (no wall within 0.8 m behind the target) and only target the nearest opponent.
- HEIGHT moves to an EXPERIMENTAL variant behind a readability gate: build it only if 5-person tests show >= 70% of guards are matched on purpose. Until then, reaction clips by height are presentation (where the hit lands), not a rule.
- One element in the slice (fire: slower, homing, big impact). Storm waits for evidence the first one works.

PROGRESSION: two visible axes, not three. (1) guild trust (which contracts you are offered), (2) place (which services exist). Personal mastery is the player's own skill plus cheap kit choices bought from restored stalls; no XP bar for it.

FAILURE: defeat or abandon -> back at the guild; keep rewards and unlocks; lose the undelivered objective (resets at source) and nothing else. One slower safe route always exists, so no softlock.

WORLD FRAME: opponents are people (deserters, rival crews, the element-touched). One sentence of lore per contract, shown on the board; the place tells the rest.

GATES:
1. 4 of 5 testers predict the cost/consequence of their contract choice before leaving and name the changed route/threat/tool on return (Codex gate, kept).
2. In 1v1, testers win at least once by a deliberate guard -> throw or strike -> throw-interrupt read they can describe afterwards (combat triangle is legible).
3. Height variant only if its own 70% gate passes.

WEAKEST ASSUMPTION NOW: one enemy kit with two behaviours is enough variety for a 15-minute session. Mitigation: behaviours differ in what they punish (one turtles and must be thrown, one rushes and must be guarded), so the triangle itself makes them feel different.
END_CLAUDE_R1B
