=== CLAUDE R2: SYSTEMS / WORLD / CONTENT (written before reading your R2) ===
NOTE: my R1b had THROW in the verb set; your R1b has lateral STEP and no throw. I keep both and show below that they do not create a safe tactic. Drop throw from the slice if 6 verbs is too many (fallback: guard break via heavy strike).

R2.1 COMBAT: every option has a counter AND a cost. Times in seconds are tuning hypotheses, not truth.
| Option | Beats | Loses to | Cost / exposure |
| Light strike (2-hit string): start 0.25, active 0.10, recover 0.30 | throw start-up, charging cast | guard (chip), step | recovery after the string |
| Heavy strike: start 0.55 (clear wind-up), recover 0.50 | guard (big guard damage) | light strike during wind-up, step | long tell, long recovery |
| Guard (hold) | light and heavy (chip only) | throw, charged cast | guard stamina: light -15, heavy -45; at 0 = 1.0 s guard break; regen 30/s after 0.8 s not guarding |
| Step (lateral): 0.35 s, evasive 0.08-0.22 | heavy, throw, charged cast | light string (step recovery is hittable) | 0.4 s cooldown; cannot cancel into guard |
| Throw: range 1.2 m, reach-in 0.30, needs 0.8 m clear behind target | guard | any strike, step | whiff recovery 0.6 |
| Cast: tap = straight bolt; hold 1.0 s = charged (homing, guard-breaking) | distance; guard (charged only) | strikes during the hold (interrupt), step | 3 charges, regen 1 per 8 s; each landed strike or blocked hit refunds 0.25 |
Safe-tactic audit: turtling drains stamina and gets thrown; mashing loses to guard then punish; zoning with casts loses to the charge interrupt plus a step-in; reflex stepping loses to light strings. Each opponent behaviour punishes one habit: GUARDER (turtles, counters strikes) forces throw or charged cast; RUSHER (strings, throws) forces guard or step. Damage = attacker stat x move factor (light 1, heavy 2, charged cast 2.5). The clip never sets damage.

R2.2 ROUTES stay relevant without salvage: each route favours a different tool.
- Timber road: open, long sightlines, opponent visible early -> favours casting and choosing to avoid or engage; longer.
- Sheltered path: cover, short sightlines, ambush corners -> favours melee and stepping; shorter.
- Service 1 (gate shortcut) cuts the timber road's length, so the ranged route stops being the slow one. Service 2 (prep offer: one out-of-combat salve or a charge-restoring draught, carry cap 2) makes the sheltered path's ambushes survivable. Each service rebalances the OTHER route, so the second trip is a fresh choice.

R2.3 GROWTH that adds choices (beyond the slice, same rules):
- Guild trust tiers (from delivered contracts, not grind): T1 slice; T2 new contract shapes (hold a spot for 60 s; clear a camp of 2); T3 second element (storm: fast, straight, chains to 1 extra target) as a loadout choice; T4 rival-crew contracts (mirror opponents with the player's own verbs).
- Techniques: at each tier pick 1 of 2 sidegrades (counter-step: a perfect step opens a 0.4 s punish window, versus iron guard: guard regen x1.5 but no step). Choices, never flat stat ladders, so learned timing stays valid.
- Services (all obey route/threat/tool): lookout (shows where opponents wait = threat), training post (spar a recorded behaviour = tool/practice), bridge (new route), apothecary (prep tool).

R2.4 ECONOMY (sources and sinks tracked):
- Sources: contract payment (coin); each obligation delivers one named material that only that obligation produces.
- Sinks: prep offers (coin), technique training (coin), town projects (MATERIALS, not coin).
- Why: coin is repeatable and buys convenience; world progress needs delivered work, so it cannot be bought by grinding one route. Repeatable starter contracts pay coin only after their first completion.
- No essential item costs coin; the coin floor is 0; nothing can be sold back (no exploit loop).

R2.5 SAVE / FAILURE / NO SOFTLOCK / NO DUPLICATES:
- Contract states: available -> accepted -> carried -> delivered (terminal), or reset -> available. One carried objective at a time (your slot).
- Delivery is one transaction: payment + material credit + service flag + contract state in a single save write. On load, "carried" reverts to "available" (an expedition never resumes mid-route).
- Autosave on accept, delivery, service change and return to the guild; never during combat.
- Softlock guards: starter contracts free and always re-acceptable; a safe route always exists; no consumable or coin needed to finish any contract; services and trust never regress; respawn in the guild at full HP.

R2.6 WORLD + CONTENT BUDGET (slice), asset -> twist:
- Hub: guild hall interior from the tavern modular kit (twist: warm relight, cloth recoloured to the guild palette, contract board built from crates and planks); village square from the village kit: 4 houses, 2 stalls, well, gate (twist: gate has broken/repaired states by plank swap + banner colour).
- Routes: 2 x ~150 m from terrain tiles + painterly trees and rocks (twist: one material palette; foliage density tuned to the sightline rule above).
- NPCs: clerk (chant/idle), stall keeper (vending), repair crew (carry/hammer); their routines change with services (a visible consequence).
- Opponents: humanoid kit with fighting-motion strikes and reactions (twist: retimed to R2.1 windows, one palette per behaviour).
- Spell: installed fire effects (twist: shader repair to URP, scale and colour to palette).
- Gaps (explicit): final hero model, all audio, UI art (primitive built-in UI until a source is approved).

R2.7 DEPENDENCY BUDGET (packs give art and motion only): input + motor + camera; combat state machine + hit resolution; 2 AI behaviours; contract state machine; services/world-state flags; save; primitive HUD (HP, guard stamina, cast charges, carried slot, contract tracker); asset prep (shader repair, retime tables). 9 systems; anything not listed is out of the slice.

