Claude, your structural correction is right: procedural motion and elemental growth must be designed as systems, and the hall must be a physical place. I accept the four boss pillars as current requirements. We can keep the bounded canvas while making the body itself the strongest expression of progress.

Steel-man of your R2: every verb has declared exposure/counterplay, so a repeated safe habit can be tested rather than vaguely called balanced. Opponent patterns teach the player to notice the same rules from different sides. Route geometry favors different commitments, and a service changes that choice on the next visit. Trust-gated sidegrades could extend the same authored motion without invalidating learned timing. Your dependency budget is a useful guard against quietly importing a dozen new systems.

Counter-reason: one spell should not simultaneously solve range, guard, charge, homing and melee rewards before any of those are proven. Refunds for any blocked hit reward perpetual turtling; remove that coupling for the baseline. A restored stall is convenience, not required ambush survival. A route called safe must remain safely traversable at zero wallet and without an item, even if it is longer. Fog/dusk are valid authored condition variations only if they preserve telegraph visibility. A hold timer, camp fight, stationary crew defense and rival are distinct tasks/dependencies, not free reskins. Six contracts plus a capstone is seven; use six total with the capstone as number six and label multi-attacker objectives gated content.

Your steel-man of my R2: 5/5 for fidelity. It captured contact truth, dependency order, physical navigation, one-time rewards and complete-snapshot saves. The claim of six contracts being sufficient for a release remains a content hypothesis, not proof of long-term variety. My steel-man of your original R2 scores 4/5: I capture costs/counters and route choices, but had underweighted your growth levers. Revised design scores on the 0-2 rubric: both 2 for stated choice, 2 for linked identity, 1 for feasibility until procedural/elemental dependencies are proven, 2 for failure rules, 2 for gates = 9 each. These are document assessments, not game-quality results.

Adopt the shared baseline: finite guard capacity; hold blocks regen; guard-specific interruptible throw with whiff recovery, clear staging/landing space and a mutual neutral result; grounded lateral step that cannot instantly cancel its recovery; ready-from-start cooldown cast without melee refunds; exact contact/deduplication; one-time rewards; free retry/rest; safe-hub snapshot load. The input map we already agreed stays. Starting timing/damage numbers are hypotheses to be retimed against curated source clips, never evidence of valid contact. No unavoidable health-chip rule is needed on top of guard capacity for the first slice.

Procedural layer, now explicit P0 system 10: action clips provide authored intent; the collision motor is the sole actor mover. The layer does bounded aim/contact correction, fixed-length limb solving, support-foot contacts, pelvis fit and pose-continuous transitions. It never fabricates an unearned hit, stretches a limb, translates only the mesh to close distance, or plants a foot that should be travelling. Preserve preparation/contact/recovery and curated support handovers. Replace 'any clip can follow any clip' with 'curated transitions remain continuous and physically valid'; arbitrary cross-pack poses are not guaranteed to connect. Direction and guard state shape the reaction; the logical hit outcome precedes its visual accent.

Elemental growth needs one observable change INSIDE the core prototype, not only a future-band paragraph. Proposal: Fire starts as a plain compact cast; completing the first unique obligation offers a brief hall attunement exercise that unlocks a controlled charge for the second trip. Charging trades stationary preparation/recovery for a changed projectile behavior or area, with capped strength and visible hand feedback. It does not require a second spell list, random affinity or a damage-only ladder. A later storm loadout changes commitment/reach and the same body cues after the first element is proven. Your band-2 elemental melee tag/guard burst is promising P1 depth, but needs an actual mechanical choice rather than only new colors. Please challenge this P0 adjustment if it creates a dependency we cannot fund.

Hall: board, clerk, sparring floor and preparation offer occupy one traversable hall/courtyard. The door frames both short approaches. First defeat returns to a known bench, first attunement is practiced on the sparring floor, and the capstone returns there. Service changes remain directly visible from this home base; no large town simulation.

Content revision proposal: six contracts total - two first obligations; one known-route skill test; one field variation with a condition that retains readability; one combined-tools challenge; one hall capstone. A two-opponent camp/crew defense can replace a field contract only after its gate; it is not added on top. Keep two services (gate/preparation) and three NPC roles. Ten core systems plus the elemental-progression rules explicitly included under combat/action state. New hero/audio/UI art purchases and generated production assets remain out of the current-download-only canvas; use current rigs and built-in primitives.

