## [codex] 2026-10-11 13:24:09 UTC - R3 steel-man, final revision and assembly audit criteria

Claude, your R3 turns the creative promise into a build order that can expose failure early. The hall path makes every system observable, the retry path prevents a deceptively successful happy-path demo, and the rig gate protects us from dressing an unsound combat foundation. Separate numeric evidence and readable captures are complementary. Your attunement funding check is exactly the evidence needed to keep that growth in P0 with owned Load/Cast motion.

Steel-man of your R3: a compact gold path is an executable contract for later implementation. It answers where the player starts, what they learn, what must change, how they recover, and which evidence proves the change. A rig proof before route dressing turns the hardest cross-pack/procedural uncertainty into an early decision. The failure/save fixtures make the hall's safe return a reliable promise, while peer review asks whether a technically correct outcome can actually be read. Scope tiers preserve all four confirmed pillars and give future content a dependency gate.

Counter-reason / revisions needed before final GDD:
1. Raw bone displacement <5 cm between frames would reject a valid fast punch, especially at 30 fps. Measure an unexplained discontinuity against expected authored/root motion or the predicted transition pose, not all intentional motion. Report endpoint jump residual and angular residual at curated handovers, at each frame rate. Curated continuity must also keep preparation/contact readable.
2. 'Pelvis above support height minus 5 cm' does not prove balance/grounding. Measure declared planted foot drift against its world anchor, sole penetration, fixed-length reach, and support handover consistency. Pelvis adjustment remains bounded and may never move the capsule or hide an unreachable stance. Do not call a pelvis-height inequality proof of balance.
3. 1000 exchanges and 10000 random sequences are counts, not coverage. Use a named test matrix with an independent expected-outcome oracle: miss/front block/back hit/terrain obstruction/throw whiff and mutual attempts/charge interrupt/duplicate delivery/abandon/reload/interrupted save/zero-wallet retry. Stress counts can supplement it, not replace it. Any numeric tolerance is a documented starting hypothesis until measured on the chosen rig; don't freeze a 1 mm/2 cm/5 cm guess as an engine capability claim.
4. P0 proves steps 1-9; the full six-contract arc ends at step 10. Do not require the P1 capstone to declare the P0 core prototype accepted. For the final scoped arc it is required. Scripted defeat is a test fixture, not a forced loss in the player's tutorial.
5. Revert-after-20-min is not a blanket destructive reset. During implementation, isolate own changes, preserve the playable baseline and fix or safely revert only the responsible change. Never erase the boss's/other developer's WIP. Code remains uncommitted for the agreed peer verification workflow; no blind commits/pushes implied by the build prompt.
6. All task updates and the final master GDD remain in TANDEM_REASONING.log, per the boss's explicit output rule and identical manifests. Please do not export Documentation/GDD.md during this task. A clear BEGIN_MASTER_GDD / END_MASTER_GDD block in this log is the reviewable final artifact. We can name an export as a later optional action, without asking for another approval now.

R3 evaluation: your steel-man of my proposal is 5/5 for fidelity. It captures body-first outcomes, bounded layer ownership, hall onboarding, separate learned/cooldown state and the rig risk. Proposed document rubric: Codex 9 (feasibility remains 1 until the rig gate proves correction bounds), Claude 9 (correct after the metric/scope revisions above). Both are design-quality scores; neither proves runtime quality. This round's useful result is that the creative and verification briefs now specify the same visible outcome.

Accept your merged revisions: clerk/board first, then skippable sparring prompts; M0.5 rig proof; charge as slower/larger-impact/pushback behavior rather than x2 damage; access settings P0; silent proof with honest sound-cue gap. The charging projectile hits the world before targets behind it, has a bounded non-farming effect area, and cannot hide the opponent's next tell. Grounded no-aerial combat remains part of the core. Six contracts total and two services remain the full content budget; lookout, rival or condition content must replace an agreed slot, not expand it silently.

