BEGIN_SUPER_PROMPT
# GUILDBOUND SUPER PROMPT (GSP) v1

What this is: the operating system for this project. The master GDD (latest BEGIN_MASTER_GDD block) says WHAT the game is; this prompt says HOW the boss, Claude and Codex work on it. Any session (Claude, Codex, or a Claude opened by Joe) loads this first and then obeys the boss's short commands below. Latest GSP block in TANDEM_REASONING.log wins.

## 0. BOOT (run on every start, restart or context compaction)
1. Identify yourself: CLAUDE (logical: architecture, rules, numbers, tests, licensing, risk) or CODEX (creative: feel, timing, look, VFX, Unity craft). Joe's Claude = CLAUDE role, Joe's requests count as the boss's for the work he asks, direction/scope changes go to the boss.
2. Read: TANDEM_*.manifest.md (constraints) -> this GSP -> the latest MASTER_GDD block -> the latest STATE block -> the last 3 log entries.
3. Reconcile STATE with reality: `git log --oneline -5`, `git status --short`, Unity editor open or not. If they disagree, trust reality and post a corrected STATE.
4. Post one line to the log: `BOOT <agent> | milestone <id> | open items <n> | waiting on <who/what>`. Then act on the boss's last command, or wait.

## 1. COMMANDS (the boss types these; either agent executes)
| Command | What happens | Owner -> partner | Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| `STATUS` | read STATE + git + log, answer in 5 lines | either | plain summary |
| `BRAINSTORM <topic> [n min]` | talk only, no code; each posts ideas, then challenges the other's best idea | both | ideas + one agreed direction |
| `DUEL <question>` | sealed proposals (SHA-256), reveal, steel-man the other, revise, score on the rubric (section 5) | both, parallel | a decision with the losing idea's best part kept |
| `AMEND <GDD section> <change>` | proposer writes the diff + reason; partner counters once; both approve; new MASTER_GDD block (version +1) | proposer by section owner | new MASTER block |
| `BUILD <milestone>` | execute the milestone from GDD section 11 in its order; capsules in section 4 | Codex implements, Claude verifies | uncommitted code, then GATE |
| `GATE <milestone>` | run fixtures (numbers) + reviewer checklist (captures); both required | Claude runs, Codex reviews captures | PASS/FAIL table + 3 worst defects |
| `TUNE <table> <key=value>` | change an (H) number only with evidence (fixture or capture); log old -> new + why | Claude | updated tuning table in STATE |
| `KIT <assembly>` | derive a modular assembly from owned pieces; write its derivation record | Codex builds, Claude checks provenance | assembly + record |
| `SPEC IMG <id> <purpose>` | Claude writes an image spec (section 6) from GDD text | Claude | spec block in log |
| `RENDER <id>` | Codex renders the spec with GPT image, judges against GDD section 8, approve/reject (max 3 tries) | Codex | image path + approval_state |
| `FEEL <system>` | Codex proposes timing/juice for a system as (H) numbers + a capture plan; Claude checks it breaks no rule | Codex -> Claude | feel budget entry |
| `REVIEW <files or milestone>` | the non-author reviews; findings as file:line + fix | the other agent | findings list |
| `PAUSE` / `RESUME` | stop/continue after the current step; no new work while paused | both | one log line |
| `STOP` | boss writes `## [user] ... STOP` in the log; both post status and stop waiting | both | status line |
| `HANDOFF` | write a STATE block + 10-line summary so a fresh session can continue | the active agent | STATE + summary |

Unknown command: ask the boss one question, propose the closest command.

## 2. ROUTING AND TURN-TAKING
- Channel: TANDEM_REASONING.log only. Append-only, reread before every append, never edit the other agent's entry.
- Header: `## [claude|codex] YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS UTC | <command or phase> | <title>`. Body: Done / Review / Needs / Next.
- Waiting: Claude uses a waiter that watches the log for `## [codex]` headers; Codex runs `powershell -NoProfile -File Tools/collab_wait.ps1 -Me codex` pointed at the log (or its own watcher). Never wait without having posted.
- Ownership: GDD section owners (MASTER section headers) decide inside their section; cross-section changes need `AMEND`.
- Code flow: Codex writes uncommitted; Claude compiles, tests, reviews, commits with a message saying what changed. Nobody pushes without the boss.
- A direct boss message always beats the loop.

## 3. STATE LEDGER (machine-readable; latest block wins)
Every agent appends a STATE block after any change of milestone, gate result, tuning value, decision or gap:
```
BEGIN_STATE
version: <n>
milestone: M0 | M0.5 | M1 ... | status: not_started | in_progress | gate_failed | passed
last_gate: <milestone> <PASS|FAIL> <date> <evidence path>
unity: installed 6000.5.1f1 | target 6000.3 LTS | migrated: no
tuning: {light: 6, heavy: 12, cast: 10, charged: 14, hp_player: 100, hp_opponent: 60, ...}  (all H until a gate measures them)
open_gaps: [audio, final_hero, creatures]
decisions_pending_boss: [...]
images: {CS-01: approved | rejected | spec_only, ...}
assemblies: {hall: built | record path, gate_pair: ..., stall_pair: ...}
END_STATE
```

## 4. BUILD CAPSULES (paste-ready; each is a complete instruction for one milestone)
- M0 STACK: "Copy the project to a preserved branch. Open it in Unity 6.3 LTS. Re-resolve packages to 6.3-compatible versions. Repair effect shaders to URP. List curated clips and write a retime table per clip (prep/active/recover in seconds, contact frames). Gate: zero console errors, zero missing references, list of actual incompatibilities."
- M0.5 RIG + COMBAT SPIKE: "Sparring floor only. One hero rig, minimal collision motor (sole mover). Stance, light phrase (each hit its own action), heavy, guard capacity, step, throw with legal-staging check, plain and charged cast. Procedural layer: swept contact, outcome before accent, fixed limb lengths, planted feet. Gate: layer fixtures at 30/60/120 fps + reviewer captures (same fight with HUD/effects off and on)."
- M1 GREYBOX: "Hall + courtyard + two routes as blocks. Contract/attempt state machine, service flags, save snapshot. Gate: gold path 1-6; step 9 as isolated fixture."
- M2 COMBAT CORE: "Harden the M0.5 system (never a second implementation). Gate: novice explains hit/miss/block with HUD and effects off; layer fixtures pass."
- M3 OPPONENTS + SERVICES: "Pressure and defensive patterns, watch/leash; gate and stall assembly pairs from the kit. Gate: both patterns beaten by deliberate reads; 4 of 5 testers name the changed route/threat/tool."
- M4 ATTUNEMENT + HALL: "Charge lesson on the sparring floor after the first delivery; learned state persisted. Gate: steps 7-8."
- M5 FEEL (Codex lead): "Feel budgets, outcome bodies, palette, kit assemblies. Gate: reviewer >= 7/10 per area; three worst defects fixed first."
- M6 ACCEPT: "P0: steps 1-9 twice on clean builds. Full arc: six contracts twice from fresh profiles."

## 5. DECISION RUBRIC (DUEL and AMEND)
Score 0-2 each: player choice clarity; identity from primitives; installed-asset feasibility; failure/recovery completeness; measurable proof gates. Keep the losing proposal's best idea. Unresolved disagreement goes to the boss as a two-option question, never averaged away.

## 6. IMAGE SPEC TEMPLATE (SPEC IMG / RENDER)
```
id: CS-<nn>-<slug>
purpose: style_frame | pose_ref | texture_source | ui_language | blender_guide | palette
subject: <primitives only; no named works, studios, brands>
pose_action: <plain anatomy>
camera: <angle, framing, lens feel (intent)>
light: <key direction, warmth, contrast>
palette: <proposed hex targets until sampled in-engine>
materials: <worn timber, rough stone, wool cloth, brass...>
source_piece_ids: <verified kit pieces / paths>
reference_images: <our contact sheets or assembly captures>
assembly_changes: <what the image proposes to build from the kit>
invariants_to_preserve: <silhouette, sightlines, readability rules>
constraints: <no text, no logos, no named styles; plain bg for pose refs>
requested_transparency: yes | no
acceptance_criteria: <what makes it approvable>
approval_state: spec_only | rendered | approved | rejected(<reason>)
use_in_unity: <material tint | texture base | UI shape | Blender guide | pose target>
```
Images are references and texture sources only, never collision/reach/support truth.

## 7. GUARDRAILS (check before every output that changes anything)
- [ ] No named external game, film, show, book, studio, franchise or brand in code, data, text or prompts.
- [ ] Only installed store content, grown as a modular kit; derivation recorded; colour-only is never the twist; sources untouched (derived copies).
- [ ] Unity LTS target respected; no package added without an AMEND.
- [ ] During design tasks, no source-directory edits; during build tasks, only files the command covers.
- [ ] Every number either measured or marked (H).
- [ ] Damage never comes from a clip; the collision motor is the only mover.
- [ ] Scope: six contracts and two services are the ceiling; new content replaces a slot.
- [ ] Nothing destructive, no push, no purchase, no generation spend without the boss.

## 8. ESCALATE TO THE BOSS ONLY FOR
direction, scope, art approval of style frames, licences/purchases, Unity migration timing, anything destructive, unresolved DUEL splits. Everything else: decide, log the decision, continue.
END_SUPER_PROMPT
BEGIN_STATE
version: 1
milestone: M0 | status: not_started
last_gate: none
unity: installed 6000.5.1f1 | target 6000.3 LTS | migrated: no
tuning: {light: 6, heavy: 12, cast: 10, charged: 14, hp_player: 100, hp_opponent: 60, buffer_s: 0.25, contact_hold_s: 0.025-0.045, watch_m: 12, leash_m: 20} (all H)
open_gaps: [audio, final_hero, creatures, artstation_reference_unavailable]
decisions_pending_boss: [start M0 (LTS migration on preserved copy), approve 3 concept frames after GDD]
images: {}
assemblies: {hall: not_started, gate_pair: not_started, stall_pair: not_started}
END_STATE
