BEGIN_KIT_LEXICON
# KIT LEXICON v1 - the whole asset library as visual building bricks

Principle (boss): every installed asset is a brick. Concept art, level building, UI and characters are all ASSEMBLIES of named bricks plus a stated twist. Nothing is drawn that the bricks cannot build. Source: Logs/sheets/{tavern,town,nature,characters,vfx_hovl,vfx_arsenal_fire_lightning}.png + .txt (contact sheets inspected 2026-10-11). Sizes and grid are UNKNOWN until measured in M0 (grid unit G, H).

## A. Visual reading of the bricks (what they actually look like)
- Village kit (V-): faceted low-poly, flat-shaded, matte, earthy. Timber houses on stone plinths, thatch/shingle roofs, crossed timber horns on gable peaks. Props are chunky, slightly crooked, hand-made feeling.
- Hall kit (T-): clean chunky modular timber, dark near-black frames, mid-brown planks, rivet dots. Wall panels currently show GREY placeholder glass/infill (material gap). Furniture matches.
- Foliage kit (A-): soft painterly clumps, bright green with yellow sun highlights, brushy silhouettes; one crimson bush. Stylistically SOFTER than V-/T- (the main style tension).
- Village vegetation/rocks (V-R, V-VEG): faceted low-poly rocks and trees, flat greens.
- Characters (C-): (1) segmented block mannequins in loud flat colours with weapon sets; (2) smooth humanoid dummies and mocap rigs (grey, red, blue, purple); one high-detail grey robot-like figure. No final hero.
- Effects (X-): element sets (fire, frost, light, lightning) x (charge, missile tiny-mega, muzzle, explosion tiny-mega, dome, shield, pillar, sphere, beam, slash hit) + generic sparks, dust, smoke, shields, portals, auras.

## B. Brick IDs
HALL KIT (T-): T-FLOOR, T-WALL, T-WIN (wall with window), T-DOOR (wall with doorway), T-POST (wall support), T-ROOF-L (line roof), T-ROOF-S (side roof), T-ROOF-CL1/CL2 (corner line roof), T-ROOF-CS1/CS2 (corner side roof); T-BAR (bar counter), T-BENCH (long bench), T-TBL-SQ, T-TBL-RD (round large), T-TBL-DIN (dining), T-STOOL, T-STOOL-TALL, T-CHAIR (backing chair), T-KEG (horizontal keg), T-BARREL (standing), T-CHEST, T-TORCH (iron bracket), T-CANDLE-1..4; tableware T-GOBLET, T-TANKARD-E/F/FAT, T-TANKARD-SPILL, T-JUG, T-BOTTLE-1/2, T-PLATE.
VILLAGE KIT (V-): V-HOUSE-01..05; V-AWN-A (blue canopy), V-AWN-B (pink canopy); V-FENCE-01A/01B (rail), V-FENCE-CNR; V-GATE-SOLID (02a plank wall), V-GATE-BROKEN (02b missing planks), V-GATE-HALF (02c); V-SHED-01/02 (thatched lean-to, 02 with bench); V-BOARDWALK-A/B; V-BANNER-A (quartered red/bone), V-BANNER-B (dark red); V-BENCH-1..3, V-CHAIR-A/B, V-BARREL-1/2, V-BASKET-1/2, V-TUB, V-BOWL, V-BOX, V-BUCKET, V-CRATE-1..3 (closed, slatted, open), V-JUG, V-PACKAGE, V-SACK-1/2, V-SACKS-SET, V-SACK-OPEN, V-TROUGH, V-VASE-1..3, V-RACK-CLOTHES, V-RACK-A, V-TRIPOD-POT, V-BROOM, V-LADDER, V-RAKE, V-POSTBOX (bird house on post), V-STONES (cut block pile), V-CART, V-WELL, V-SHIELD-1/2 (wall shields), V-TABLE, V-LOGS-1..3.
NATURE (V-R/V-VEG/TER-/A-): V-ROCK-1..3, V-ROCK-S1/S2, V-PEBBLES; TER-GRASS-1/2, TER-PATH-A/B, TER-SAND, HILL-1/2, MTN-1, SKY-DOME, CLOUD-1/2; V-BUSH-1/2, V-FLOWER-R/Y/B, V-GRASS-1/2, V-PLANT-1/2, V-TREE-1/2, V-PINE; A-TREE-1..8, A-BUSH-1 (crimson), A-BUSH-2..4, A-GRASS-1/2.
CHARACTERS (C-): C-MOCAP (rig_MCUnity), C-BLUE, C-RED, C-DUMMY-M, C-DUMMY-F, C-MORRO, C-BLOCK-* (block mannequins: brute, karate, ninja, sorceress, 2h, archer, knight, mage, crossbow, hammer, spearman, swordsman, crafter, berserker, heavy).
EFFECTS (X-): X-FIRE-{CHARGE, MISSILE-T/S/N/M, MUZZLE-N/B, EXPLODE-T/S/N/M, DOME, SHIELD, PILLAR, SPHERE, BEAM, SLASHHIT, ORBIT, GLOW}; same for FROST, LIGHT, LIGHTNING; X-SPARK-*, X-DUST-{PUFF, GROUND, LOOP}, X-SMOKE-*, X-SHIELD-*, X-PORTAL-*, X-AURA-LIGHTNING, X-HIT-{ELECTRO, EXPLOSION, STONES}, X-SLASH-*.

## C. Assembly grammar (how bricks snap)
- BAY = T-POST + one infill (T-WALL | T-WIN | T-DOOR) + T-POST. Bays chain along a line; posts are shared.
- ROOF RUN = T-ROOF-L over each bay, T-ROOF-S on gable sides, T-ROOF-CL/CS at corners. A building = closed ring of bays + roof run.
- THRESHOLD = 2 T-POST at 1.3-1.5x height (proportion edit) + T-ROOF-L as a lintel canopy + a banner pair. Marks every important doorway.
- SERVICE EDGE = counter brick (T-BAR or V-TABLE) + storage brick (T-CHEST/V-CRATE) + a vertical marker (V-RACK or T-TORCH). Every service has one.
- STATE PAIR = the same assembly in two states built from the SAME bricks: damaged (missing/tilted pieces, props piled, no light, no cloth) vs restored (aligned pieces, cloth, light, an NPC routine). Growth is always a state pair.
- LANDMARK = one tall or bright silhouette per space (well, cart, banner, gate frame, pine) visible from the hall door.
- PALETTE LAW: wood from the kits stays; cloth and banners carry guild colour; stone stays cool grey; foliage is tuned toward the palette; effects stay saturated but small.
- Proportion edits allowed on derived copies: uniform scale 0.8-1.5x, single-axis stretch for posts/beams, piece removal/duplication (mesh edits), material derivatives. Never colour-only.

## D. Recipes (assemblies for the GDD content)
1. GUILD HALL "long hall": 3 x 5 bay ring; front gable: T-DOOR centre, T-WIN either side; roof run complete; THRESHOLD at the front door with V-BANNER-A pair; crossed gable horns kitbashed from V-HOUSE roof peaks onto the hall gable (mesh edit) so hall and village read as one people. Inside: SERVICE EDGE = T-BAR + T-KEG + T-CHEST (clerk); board = freestanding T-WALL between two T-POST with primitive paper quads; long T-BENCH rows; T-TORCH + T-CANDLE for warm pools of light; a rear T-DOOR to the sparring floor.
2. SPARRING FLOOR (courtyard): TER-PATH tiles as packed earth; ring of V-FENCE-01; V-BOARDWALK on one edge for watchers on V-BENCH; V-SHIELD-1/2 hung on the fence as trophies; V-RACK-A with practice gear; LANDMARK: V-POSTBOX post with the guild banner.
3. GATE PAIR: damaged = V-GATE-BROKEN in a frame of two T-POST, V-STONES and V-LOGS piled, V-LADDER leaning, no light; restored = V-GATE-SOLID (open leaf) in the same frame, lintel T-ROOF-L, V-BANNER-B, T-TORCH lit, path cleared to a shorter route.
4. STALL PAIR: dormant = V-SHED-01, stacked V-CRATE-3, V-SACKS-SET, V-BROOM, no cloth; active = V-AWN-A recoloured guild bone/red over V-TABLE, V-BASKET-1/2, V-JUG, V-VASE-1..3 (prep items), V-RACK-CLOTHES, stall keeper NPC with vending routine.
5. EXPOSED TIMBER ROAD: TER-PATH strip, V-FENCE-01 runs with gaps, V-CART abandoned mid-road, V-LOGS piles, low V-BUSH only (long sightlines), one V-PINE landmark at the far end; recovery site: V-SHED-02 + V-CRATE-1 (tool crate) + V-RAKE + V-LADDER.
6. SHELTERED PATH: A-TREE clusters close to the path, V-ROCK-1..3 as cover and ambush corners, A-BUSH-1 crimson accent at the turn, A-GRASS; recovery site: V-SACK set + V-BASKET + V-TROUGH under trees.
7. OPPONENT POST (watch/leash anchor): V-TRIPOD-POT + V-LOGS + V-SACK-OPEN + V-BARREL; readable from a distance by the smoke loop (X-SMOKE-LOOP small).

## E. Style directions to decide with concept frames (boss chooses)
- SD-A "CARVED FOLK": everything reads as carved timber and stone with matte painted pigment; facets are deliberate chisel planes; characters are faceted figures that belong in the faceted village (bridges the block mannequins, V- kit and T- kit). Foliage is tuned to fewer, larger leaf clumps. Strength: one coherent world from what we own. Risk: foliage pack fights it unless retuned.
- SD-B "PAINTED SOFT": buildings and props get soft hand-painted gradients and brush texture derived from the foliage pack; characters smooth (mocap rigs) with painted materials. Strength: lush, warm. Risk: the faceted kits need heavy material work to stop looking flat.
Recommendation (Claude): SD-A primary, with A- foliage as the one soft element at the edges of decision spaces (Codex's existing rule). Codex owns the call to the boss.

## F. Palette (proposed targets, sampled from bricks; verify in-engine)
timber dark #4A3122 | timber mid #7A5233 | timber light #B38552 | frame near-black #2A211C | stone #8C8A85 | stone dark #55534F | thatch #9C9268 | guild madder red #8E2F25 (from V-BANNER-A) | guild bone #E6DAC2 (from V-BANNER-A) | grass #6E9A4A | sun foliage #C9D85A | sky #9FB2C8 | fire core #FFD27A | fire edge #E2561F | torch pool #F2A65A.

