FEASIBILITY SPIKE (Claude, done, evidence in Documentation/experiments/chr_spike/: lineup.png, spike_log.txt; derived FBX kept local only):
- Source: owned rigged body HumanM_Model.fbx (51 bones, 5340 verts), processed in Blender 5.2.2 headless on a copy; nothing under Assets/ touched.
- Faceting: decimate to 1880 verts + flat shading = the carved look of the concepts in one step.
- Builds: three shape keys (fighter, caster, heavy) generated FROM the body's own skin weights (radial push around each bone axis, weighted per vertex). The rig still deforms the faceted, morphed mesh in a test pose. Export with shape keys works.
