=> Verdict: the owned body CAN be the base of a creator and of trained builds. Clothing/hair remain the separate gap (derived mesh pieces, see my previous entry).

PROPOSED DESIGN (Claude rules; Codex owns look and creator UX):
1. CREATOR AXES (all on one derived owned body per sex; Humanoid retarget unaffected):
   - Build blend: weights over fighter / caster / heavy / lean shape keys (sum <= 1).
   - Proportion: height via uniform root scale 0.92-1.08; shoulder width and limb thickness via shape keys only (never bone-length edits, so every clip stays valid).
   - Head: faceless faceted head; 4-6 head-shape keys + hair caps (derived rigid pieces).
   - Palette: skin tone and outfit colours from the palette set; guild red reserved for the sash.
2. TRAINED SPECIALISATION ("you become what you train"):
   - Each body has a build_state vector (fighter, caster, heavy). Training sources move it slowly: completed contracts by how they were won (strikes/throws landed vs casts landed vs guard capacity absorbed), sparring-floor lessons, the attunement.
   - Rate: at most +0.08 per delivered contract per axis, cap 1.0; it never decreases (progress never regresses); the creator sets the starting point.
   - Visible markers per path: fighter = broader shoulders/forearms + wraps tier; caster = leaner build + ember scars along the forearms (texture layer) + hand glow at rest; heavy = thicker torso/legs + padded layer.
   - FAIRNESS RULE: the build is presentation. Collision capsule and limb contact volumes are FIXED per bone regardless of morph, so a bigger body never hits further or gets hit easier. Stats come from CombatStats, never from the mesh.
3. DEPTH MAPS (where they help, honestly):
   - Concept image -> depth map -> (a) relief/normal detail baked onto the faceted low-poly cloth (folds, stitching) as a material derivative; (b) a sculpt guide for clothing volumes in Blender; (c) creator thumbnails.
   - Tool gap: GPT image does not produce measured depth. A depth-estimation tool is needed (a Higgsfield model if one exists in its catalog, or a local depth estimator). TOOL CHOICE = BOSS DECISION. Depth output is a detail source only, never geometry truth.
4. PIPELINE (repeatable script, extends the spike): owned body -> facet -> build keys with seam-safe falloff -> clothing/hair derived pieces -> texture layers (palette + depth-baked detail + path markers) -> export to a derived folder -> Humanoid avatar check -> M0.5 deformation gate (8 combat + 4 cast poses, clipping tolerance).
5. SCOPE: creator + trained builds are a P1 feature on top of the P0 slice, except the base faceted hero body which is P0 (needed for the rig proof). Fits the GDD's growth rule: growth adds a visible change, never a hidden multiplier.

